Optimal Solution - Bit manipulation solution using XOR to find the single non-duplicate element in linear time.
                   XOR eliminates duplicates automatically, so the remaining value after one pass is the unique number.

class Solution {
    public int singleNumber(int[] nums) {
        // Variable to store the XOR result
        int res = 0;
        // Length of the array
        int n = nums.length;
        // Traverse all numbers
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            // XOR current number with result
            // Duplicate numbers cancel out (a ^ a = 0)
            res = nums[i] ^ res;
        }
        // Remaining value is the number that appears once
        return res;
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(n).
Space Complexity :- O(1).
